  "body": "## Summary\n\n- carry an explicit completed `fix-pr` pass count through the orchestration workflow chain\n- increment the count only after an actual `fix-pr` action returns to the orchestrator\n- enforce the one-pass limit in deterministic handoff code instead of asking the planner to infer history from rounds or comments\n- expose the authoritative count to the planner and document that round number is not fix history\n- add regressions for the observed `implement → review` round-3 path and the real post-fix review limit\n\n## Context\n\nPR #498 added a prompt-only one-pass rule. On PR #501, the round-3 post-review planner incorrectly inferred that a fix pass had already happened and silently stopped, even though the chain was only `orchestrate → implement → review`.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `npm --prefix .agent run test:ci`\n- `git diff --check`\n",
